176945978,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":93.6,"_gate_pool_share":-0.10853901990830206,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.014806537809704645,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":32.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.09730336858925881,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.000107376056745348,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":50.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08915093914964738,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.00022123757563052848,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":49.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.44841,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Westlake Chemical Partners LP acquires, develops, and operates ethylene production facilities and related assets in the United States. It's ethylene production facilities which primarily convert ethane into ethylene. The company also sells ethylene co-products, such as propylene, crude butadiene, pyrolysis gasoline, and hydrogen directly to third parties on either a spot or contract basis. It serves as the general partner of the company. Westlake Chemical Partners LP was founded in 1991 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jean-Marc  Gilson | President, CEO & Director of Westlake Chemical Partners GP LLC | Age 62","financial_summary":["Westlake Chemical Partners LP is a small-cap basic materials business with a $747M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -10% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Gross margins of 36% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $202M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.76\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 8.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 45% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"tex